---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
import Picture from '../../components/Picture.astro';
import { images } from '../../data/images';

/*
 * Stylist directory. With one stylist, the full profile is presented directly.
 * The structure below (stable slug, portrait, introduction, story, specialties,
 * services) is ready to become a portrait list when real collaborators join,
 * without redesigning the About structure. Menu label then becomes
 * "Our Hairstylists"; the route stays /about/hairstylists.
 *
 * Biography source: the personal-story material preserved in the master brief
 * (Feedback MC.com homepage.key). The owner's display name and current
 * qualification wording are open items; see _handoff/HANDOFF.md.
 */
const specialties = [
  'Haircuts and curly haircuts',
  'Grey-hair transitions',
  'Hair care and recovery',
  'Coaching alongside hairdressing',
  'On-location services',
];
---

<Base
  title="About the Hairstylist"
  description="Meet the hairstylist and founder of Maison Coiffure: entrepreneur, intercultural consultant and coach turned hairstylist, blending hairstyling with coaching in a personal home salon."
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="About"
    title="About the Hairstylist"
    lede="A journey full of unexpected twists and turns, defined by trying new things and taking risks."
    crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }, { label: 'About the Hairstylist' }]}
  />

  <div class="wrap section">
    <div class="split" style="align-items: start;">
      <div>
        <div class="photo-frame" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;">
          <Picture image={images.stylistPortrait} sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 45vw" loading="eager" />
        </div>
        <div class="note-box" style="margin-top: 20px;">
          <h4>Specialties</h4>
          <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 18px;">
            {specialties.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p style="margin-top: 14px;">
            <a class="arrow-link" href="/book">
              Book an appointment
              <svg class="arrow" width="18" height="12" viewBox="0 0 18 12" aria-hidden="true" fill="none"><path d="M1 6h15M11.5 1.5 16.5 6l-5 4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <article class="prose" id="my-story">
        <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">My Story</h2>
        <p>
          There's something quietly powerful about a fresh haircut or style. As Coco Chanel once
          said, "A woman who cuts her hair is about to change her life." A new cut, colour, or
          treatment can boost confidence, inspire change, mark a new chapter in life, or simply
          celebrate it. This transformation, both inside and out, mirrors the way I approach my
          work, helping individuals and businesses navigate change with clarity and confidence.
        </p>
        <p>
          My journey has been full of unexpected twists and turns, but it has always been defined by
          trying new things and taking risks. I am not for nothing an entrepreneur at heart, guided
          by curiosity, strategic thinking, and a passion for fostering collaboration. In 2014, I
          co-founded THEY VISUALIZE VALUE in India, a brand consulting and marketing agency, and
          became the Managing Director. Since then, I have played a key role in driving the
          strategic and financial growth of the company, ensuring smooth business operations,
          supporting team development, and overseeing high-level content creation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Through my work, I gradually became involved in intercultural consultancy, a field I
          hadn't initially set out to pursue but naturally evolved into. Having lived in India for
          six years and worked there for over 14 years, I've witnessed firsthand the challenges of
          cross-cultural collaboration. As I worked with European and Indian teams struggling to
          understand one another, I found myself in the middle: listening, advising, and bridging
          cultural gaps. Now, I support businesses and individuals navigating cultural complexities,
          whether it's expats adapting to new work environments or multinational teams striving for
          smoother collaboration.
        </p>
        <p>
          While I continue to lead THEY, now in The Netherlands, my passion for helping people
          navigate change has expanded beyond the corporate world. I am currently training to become
          a registered therapist and coach, with certification expected in 2027. This step felt like
          a natural progression from my consulting work, allowing me to help individuals through
          personal, professional, and cultural transitions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most recently, I embarked on a hairstyling certification at the Nederlands
          Kappersakademie, where I discovered a unique opportunity to blend hairstyling with
          coaching. At Maison Coiffure, I offer bespoke hair transformations paired with tailored
          coaching sessions, helping clients embrace both their inner and outer changes with
          confidence.
        </p>
        <p>
          Whether in business operations, intercultural consultancy, coaching, or hairstyling, my
          goal remains the same: to empower people through change, ensuring they have the tools,
          clarity, and confidence to navigate life's transitions with ease.
        </p>

        <p style="margin-top: 2em;">
          <a class="arrow-link" href="/about/philosophy">
            What that means for your appointment: the MC Philosophy
            <svg class="arrow" width="18" height="12" viewBox="0 0 18 12" aria-hidden="true" fill="none"><path d="M1 6h15M11.5 1.5 16.5 6l-5 4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
